=== start ===
# checkpoint: start
The glow fills the windshield, then the cab, then the inside of your eyelids. Closing them changes nothing. # place: The breach
It isn't even hot. That's the strange part. Through the link the truck feels whole, the way it always does: a clean sense of steel, rubber and diesel at the edge of everything. The engine is fine. The tires are fine.
It's you that's wrong. Your hands have gone soft and far away, and there's iron in your mouth. # page
The link has always known where you end. A row of contacts down your spine, a plug at the base of your skull, two clamps at your neck, and the truck on the other side of them, sure of who sits in its seat.
Now it starts to lose you. Its sense of you flickers, the way a radio drifts off a station. It reaches for the hands on the wheel and finds them, and then it doesn't. It reaches for the breath in the seat and finds less of it every time.
Somewhere in the back of your head a sense you never had a name for goes quiet. # page
The light lies across the seat, the wheel and the slack hands on it. The engine idles.
For a long time the truck waits for its driver to come back into the link. Nobody does. There is no driver in the seat now, only a body. # reveal: word
The engine idles until the tank runs dry.
-> END
